# Castlevania: Curse of Darkness (4B4E002D), FIRST RUN: no save on the disk.
# PLAYED by nav.py on the Nova, 2026-10-01 14:18 PDT (lane.titleroutes HELD
# session castlevania-cod.first-run-20261001T141851, the owner-approved
# one-time Nova path-finding session, #397).
#
# Replaces the two earlier drafts, neither ever played past a menu:
# lane.routeprep's all-[guess] draft (adopted session 42, never replayed) and
# the generic `--route survey`-derived castlevania-cod.route (session 48,
# Thor, heat-stopped at 284/300s, never confirmed by a real replay). The
# trap both missed: NEW GAME's Name Entry keyboard needs an explicit jump to
# "Accept" (press START, which jumps the cursor there on this keyboard; A
# alone leaves the cursor on the letter grid), and the save-data prompt
# right after defaults its cursor to "No" (axis LX min moves it onto "Yes"
# before A, or the route declines its own save and loops back to Name
# Entry).
#
#   intro FMV (A) -> title, New Game (A) -> Name Entry: A types the
#   highlighted "A", START jumps the cursor to Accept, A accepts -> "Is this
#   correct?" (A, Yes already selected) -> "There is no save data... Create
#   new save data?" (LX min moves the cursor from the default No onto Yes,
#   then A) -> "Creating new save data..." -> save slot list, slot 1
#   highlighted (A) -> "Saving..." -> the opening cutscene (1476, Valachia;
#   A three times, 5.4s apart, clears the castle-exterior shots) -> player
#   control in a gothic courtyard facing a gargoyle fountain.
#
# Player control confirmed by eye: LY min visibly closed the distance to the
# fountain between two shots taken 1.5s apart (014-moved.png), then the play
# pattern (LY min/press A/RX sweep) walked him along the fountain's edge and
# into an attack animation (016-postplay.png). HP bar steady at 100/100
# throughout -- no combat pressure this early.
#
# NOT YET REPLAYED UNATTENDED: played only by nav.py's interactive steps, not
# by `route.sh` reading this file end to end. Treat as a draft until a soak
# or scratch/replay.sh run confirms the same path from a cold launch.
